{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2132 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7f9d522e71348cfcd1177d59c7ae5d6391d628c9f9f49a8a42360935242d2477" :edb/db-before-t 2131 :edb/db-after-t 2132 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535444 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:12:45.003Z" 13194139535444 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349365 13194139535444 true] [17592186087753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349372 13194139535444 true] [17592186087753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349381 13194139535444 true] [17592186330960 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139535444 false] [17592186330960 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349366 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1089 "q-104487" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1100 "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $f(x).$" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1113 #uuid "9170fbba-1982-59c3-8508-b90dfbe3f341" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349365 1145 "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-5))(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{3}+9x+5{x}^{2}+45) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135.$" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349367 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349368 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349369 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349370 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349371 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1041 "selection" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349368 13194139535444 true] [17592186349366 1110 #uuid "add77e9f-1fc2-5826-8f5e-485eed64598e" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349367 1034 "3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}-27x-135" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349367 1111 #uuid "6a452fa5-62a5-5134-98d9-60a2b660c183" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349368 1034 "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349368 1111 #uuid "a7d63e91-fbea-59ab-8a62-0ec54f31eb0d" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349369 1034 "3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+27x-45" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349369 1111 #uuid "0ea7cbfa-12a4-5282-8081-001e4d5c494a" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349370 1034 "3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-9x+70" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349370 1111 #uuid "5bc0cd64-fa7a-5451-b312-4274ac904b73" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349371 1034 "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+18x+45" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349371 1111 #uuid "d5b14b46-8de5-58ab-85b8-a53b7786468d" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349373 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349375 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349377 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349379 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1089 "q-275173" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,{x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1113 #uuid "ef8fa624-35e8-5857-85ad-f8bc134682e7" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349372 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=3,$ ${x}_{2}=3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-3)(x-3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-3)(x-3)(x-4) & =2({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}+24x+9x-36) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+33x-36) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}+66x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}+66x-72.$" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349374 13194139535444 true] [17592186349373 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535444 true] [17592186349373 1041 "field-1" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349373 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349374 13194139535444 true] [17592186349373 1110 #uuid "93f53fae-08ec-55d7-bc22-60cad6d1af91" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349374 1034 "2" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349374 1111 #uuid "f7a