1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535444 true] [17592186349381 1100 "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349381 1113 #uuid "895764df-0dac-5f6c-8455-f03cf4d8e10f" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349381 1145 "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-4(x-5)(x-(-2))(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2) & =-4(x-5)({x}^{2}+4x+4) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+4x-5{x}^{2}-20x-20) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.$" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349383 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349384 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1041 "field-1" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349383 13194139535444 true] [17592186349382 1110 #uuid "67b3ae0e-24ac-5ad5-b028-05b035374677" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349383 1034 "-4" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349383 1111 #uuid "e09d4ea0-ea16-5134-9f75-9ef0ccfd2276" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349384 1034 "4" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535444 true] [17592186349384 1111 #uuid "d382bb22-1fc7-5299-b26d-dae99accb4d6" 13194139535444 true] [17592186349385 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349386 13194139535444 true] [17592186349385 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535444 true] [17592186349385 1041 "field-